# <TICKET-ID>: <ticket title> — test plan

Filled in by the test-author during the `test` phase, before writing any test. `tools/story-gate`'s `TraceabilityCheck` reads this file and requires every live criterion's full ID (`<TICKET-ID>.AC-<n>`) to appear in it somewhere, so keep the ID column exact. Delete this instruction line and every `<...>` placeholder before committing.

## Criterion → scenario → test

| Criterion | Scenario | Test (`@DisplayName`) |
|---|---|---|
| `<TICKET-ID>.AC-1` | `<scenario title from the ticket>` | `<TICKET-ID>.AC-1 <short readable title>` |
| ... | ... | ... |

One row per scenario; a criterion with several scenarios gets several rows. A test whose display name proves more than one criterion lists every ID it starts with, comma-separated, e.g. `<TICKET-ID>.AC-1, <TICKET-ID>.AC-2 <title>` (see `test-guide.md`).

## Fakes and fixtures used

- `<port or seam>`: faked with `<fake implementation, e.g. a scripted runner that emits chosen events, blocks on a latch, returns a chosen result or throws>`
- Executor: `<a manual executor that queues tasks until the test runs them, or a real virtual-thread executor for the one real-thread test>`
- Fixture files: `<from file-scanner/src/test/resources/fixtures/, or generated in code — name which and why>`

## Notes for the implementer

Anything a test relies on that is not obvious from its name (the exact event a fake blocks at, the order two transitions are applied in, a bounded timeout's length). Empty section ("None.") if there is nothing to add.
